Division, simd, indirect branches are not supported?

I am worried that a jump table is a common thing that can appear in compiler output or assembly
 [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Branch_table](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Branch_table) ,
  especially on some architectures. This would require some indirect jump support.
   Also maybe the ability to read global memory? I'm also concerned that some assembly tweaks global symbols
   that also might need to be visible / tweaked from C ? Maybe we've bitten off too much and this just won't be easily
   supportable without too much added complication ?


