Are we fundametnally restricted by the goto binary based infrasturcture. Some things it would be nice to iteratively discover?
What are alternatives to this architecture?
Is there some way to do it better? It feels like one ought to be able to link assembly binaries against C files, but it isn't easy for us?
Would a binary specific static analysis help some issues? Resolving jump possibilities, etc. How to do so soundly?
Preexisting C++ binary analysis tooling? C? Reuse more out of ghidra?

Going between assembly and C is an FFI boundary basically. Perhaps we should take more qeueus from such designs

It would be good to validate executions against concrete executions on qemu / native as part of our tests.
Pcode semantics and our interpretation of it is not entirely trustworthy. Fuzzing

Is it really not possible to hand cbmc memory objects over into the assembly?
Could we not interpret ghidra LOAD and STORE instruction using the same memory model as the C layer uses (split the pointer inter object identifier and offset)?
We could also allocate a ram block as a stack (as a cbmc object)
Detecting misuse of C provided malloced (out of bounds etc) objects would be a great bug finding thing.
Maybe I'm wrong that this ought to be fairly possible but let's think about it

Information leakage checking? Self comparison letting high data differ but low data is the same. Should just be a harness?
Binsec examples?

Maybe instead of just instruction count, could count loads,stores,arith ops ?
Something useful to do with taint?

CBAT had other effects observed. What is written to or read from can be an effect of interest. What functions are called.

SAIL has a much better fine grained model. Would we be able to detect unaligned loads and stores? Other issues like that are not persay part of the
pcode output. Some things depend on the current machine state in a way that the pcode lifters make optimisitc assumptions?
You could look at the sail-graham project for more stuff like this.
How feasible would it be to use sail or isla output in addition to or instead of pcode?
Pcode does make it easy being a prepackaged C++ project.
